{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Calls the spy’s method, expecting it to throw an error."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/documentation\/SwiftMocking","doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/documentation\/SwiftMocking\/Spy"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@discardableResult","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"callAsFunction","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"input","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": repeat each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Input","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fileID","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"StaticString","preciseIdentifier":"s:s12StaticStringV"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"#fileID"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"filePath"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"StaticString","preciseIdentifier":"s:s12StaticStringV"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"#filePath"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"line"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UInt","preciseIdentifier":"s:Su"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"#line"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"column"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UInt","preciseIdentifier":"s:Su"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"#column"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Output"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"input","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The arguments for the method call.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The output of the method if it doesn’t throw.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When invoked directly (rather than through a generated conformance) the defaulted"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"location parameters capture the caller’s own file and line, so a failure raised"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"here is attributed to the calling test."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"unstubbed"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" call reports and then traps, rather than throwing. The requirement","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"being able to throw gives SwiftMocking somewhere to put the error, but a missing"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"stub is a test-authoring mistake rather than a condition under test, and a bare"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throw hides it whenever the caller catches broadly — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"type":"text","text":", or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"catch"},{"type":"text","text":" that maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every error to a default. That turns a missing stub into a test passing against a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value the mock never produced."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Trapping matches how the non-throwing effects already treat the same mistake, so","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every unstubbed call behaves alike regardless of the requirement’s effects. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reportUnrecoverable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"stubbed","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" error propagates normally, since that is the behavior under test."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The error thrown by the method.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Throws","type":"aside","style":"note"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_transparent"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@inlinable"},{"type":"text","text":": this variant surfaces an unstubbed call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a thrown error rather than a trap, but a stubbed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"thenThrow"},{"type":"text","text":" handler or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered action can still trap, and the frame must not be SwiftMocking’s. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reportUnrecoverable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftmocking\/spy\/callasfunction(_:fileid:filepath:line:column:)-48el5"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/documentation\/SwiftMocking\/Spy\/callAsFunction(_:fileID:filePath:line:column:)-48el5","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Effects","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Throws","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"externalID":"s:12SwiftMocking3SpyCA2A6ThrowsORs_rlE14callAsFunction_6fileID0H4Path4line6columnq0_xxQp_s12StaticStringVALS2utKF","modules":[{"name":"SwiftMocking"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ca